# .confidential-terms.example — copy to ".confidential-terms" and fill in.
#
# The real file is GITIGNORED and must never be committed. It holds the
# literal strings that may not appear in tracked files. The release gate
# (tools/check-confidentiality.mjs) loads it and fails on any match; when the
# file is absent, as in CI, the structural rules still run.
#
# One term per line, case-insensitive. Blank lines and #-comments ignored.
# When the gate reports a hit it names the file and line but NEVER quotes the
# term, so its output stays safe to paste anywhere.
#
# Keep terms specific. A term as short and common as "acme" will match inside
# unrelated words and bury you in false positives.
#
# Every example below is INVENTED. Replace them.

# --- employer, and forms of its name ---
# examplecorp
# example corp

# --- internal infrastructure: gateway/service names, hosts, IPs, ports ---
# gw-example-01
# gateway.example.internal          confidentiality-allow
# 10.20.30.40                       confidentiality-allow

# --- internal Slack channels ---
# #eng-example-team

# --- people and work email ---
# firstname.lastname@examplecorp.com

# --- client / site / building identifiers ---
# SITE-001
# 1234 Example Street               confidentiality-allow

# --- real document filenames shared for debugging ---
# Example_Remediation_Report.docx
